---

<AudienceLanding {...page}>
  <section slot="after-solution" class="section carer-partner-network" aria-labelledby="carer-partner-network-title">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading audience-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow dark">Promotion, signposting and referral</p>
          <h2 id="carer-partner-network-title">Turn every trusted partner into a doorway to carer support.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>Bridgit helps schools, GPs, employers and VCSE organisations recognise carers, respond confidently and connect them into your service—without expecting every partner to become a carer specialist.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="carer-partner-layout">
        <ol class="carer-partner-flow">
          <li><span>01</span><div><h3>Promote and identify</h3><p>Share real case studies, campaign materials, QR codes and audience-specific messages through the networks carers already trust.</p></div></li>
          <li><span>02</span><div><h3>Train the wider network</h3><p>The partner portal explains caring roles, common signs and the practical steps a school, GP, employer or community organisation can take.</p></div></li>
          <li><span>03</span><div><h3>Guide the immediate response</h3><p>Partners receive targeted advice for the specific carer in front of them, helping them respond appropriately while staying within their role.</p></div></li>
          <li><span>04</span><div><h3>Signpost or refer</h3><p>An integrated referral route connects the carer to additional digital support through Bridgit or directly to your team when personal help is needed.</p></div></li>
        </ol>

        <aside class="carer-partner-portal" aria-label="Illustrative Bridgit partner portal">
          <div class="partner-portal-header"><span>Bridgit partner portal</span><strong>Young carer support</strong></div>
          <div class="partner-portal-card"><small>Learn</small><h3>Could this young person be a carer?</h3><p>Recognise common signs and understand how caring can affect school, wellbeing and family life.</p></div>
          <div class="partner-portal-card"><small>Act</small><h3>How can we help today?</h3><p>Receive practical, role-appropriate guidance shaped around the young person’s situation.</p></div>
          <div class="partner-portal-referral"><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><div><strong>Connect to further support</strong><p>Refer into Bridgit or request support from the carer service.</p></div></div>
        </aside>
      </div>

      <div class="carer-partner-outcome"><strong>Partners are empowered to act.</strong><span>Carers receive help earlier.</span><span>Your service remains connected to every journey.</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</AudienceLanding>
